      en: "Nuwakot Durbar is a historic palace complex in Nuwakot, Nepal, about 75 km northwest of Kathmandu. It was built in the 18th century under the Malla dynasty and later used by the Shah dynasty after Prithvi Narayan Shah captured Nuwakot in 1744. The palace is an example of traditional Newar architecture with courtyards and woodcarvings. It served as a military outpost and trading center on the route to Tibet. The complex includes multiple courtyards (chowks) and temples. The palace was expanded in the 19th century. After the 2015 earthquake, it was restored. Today, it is a museum showcasing Nepalese history and art.",
