      en: "Janaki Mandir in Janakpur, Nepal, is a Hindu temple dedicated to the goddess Sita. The current temple was built in 1911 in Mughal-Indian style, made of white marble and stone. It stands 22 meters high and has 60 rooms. The temple is a major pilgrimage site as Janakpur is believed to be Sita's birthplace. The temple grounds include a large courtyard and several smaller shrines. The temple was rebuilt in the 19th century after a fire. Annually, hundreds of thousands of pilgrims attend the Vivah Panchami festival, celebrating the marriage of Rama and Sita. The temple is a masterpiece of Hindu temple architecture in Nepal.",
